EVALUATION.md §1, DECISIONS 331: a broken check breaks its record (DECISIONS 209); the one value
typed by it is not evaluated or checked, so one W4001 (one) at the record says so. `w`, which
only reads that value, is silent and not counted.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Gem.
record Gem {
  /// Weight.
  weight: Int

  check light: weight < 5 else "heavy"

  check broken: weight < "5" else "broken"
}

/// Fails light, but Gem is broken.
let heavy: Gem = { weight: 9 }

/// Reads heavy: silenced, not counted.
let w: Int = heavy.weight / 0
-- findings.txt --
warning[W4001]  a/a.canon:5:8
  1 value was not evaluated or checked because a.Gem is broken: fix the errors in it or in the types it names

error[E3310]  a/a.canon:11:17
  < needs an orderable type, found String

1 error, 1 warning in 1 package (…)
